Below is a brief description of what’s happening and the minimal set of edits required to eliminate the DAP errors you’re seeing.

1) Bug Root Cause  
  – The input is always rendered with  
    aria-controls="…__menu"  
    even when the listbox isn’t present in the DOM, so you get “invalid ID” violations.  
  – The outer combobox container (<ListBox.Field role="combobox">) never actually picks up the consumer’s aria-label (it always self-labels “Open menu” / “Close menu”), so you also see “interactive element must have an accessible name.”  

2) Fixes  
  • Only set aria-controls on the input when the menu is open  
  • Pass the consumer’s aria-label (ariaLabel prop) through to the <ListBox.Field>  
  • Tweak the default aria-label logic in ListBoxField so a consumer-provided aria-label wins  

